.TH AWSV4TEST 1
.SH NAME
awsv4test \- test AWS Signature Version 4 signing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B awsv4test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Awsv4test
checks
.IR awsv4 (2)'s
signing against authoritative vectors, offline \(em no network, no
AWS account. It first checks the building blocks (the empty-body
SHA-256, a known SHA-256, and vector 1's canonical-request hash), so
a failure points at which stage broke rather than only at the final
signature.
.PP
Vector 1 is AWS's own
.B aws-sig-v4-test-suite
.B get-vanilla
case \(em the canonical published example, whose expected signature
.RB ( 5fa00fa3\c
.BR ...\c
.BR 763fbf31 )
is both documented by AWS and reproduced independently by
.BR botocore ;
the test was written against that agreement, not a single source.
Vector 2 adds an out-of-order query string (exercising the
canonical-query sort and percent-encoding) and a non-empty payload,
with the expected signature computed from the same spec by a separate
implementation.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/awsv4test.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR awsv4 (2),
.IR s3 (1),
.IR s3test (1)
.SH BUGS
The negative controls \(em flipping one byte of the secret, of
.IR amzdate ,
or of the signing-key derivation, each of which must change the
signature \(em are run by editing the source, not automated, since
they require corrupting the library. Coverage is the two vectors
above plus the building-block hashes; presigned-URL and
streaming-payload signing are unimplemented and untested (see
.IR awsv4 (2)'s
own BUGS).
